:true,"_score_int_coverage":16.7,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":2.4679611650485436,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":34.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.03566258718252402,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":32.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.09484957233680082,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":87.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.03870375107675088,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":51.6,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.01755833252533462,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":8.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.2739599033503289,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":54.3,"_gate_incr_roic":0.28124191059983217,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.04947131885511817,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":49.8,"_gate_pool_share":0.08391305885482159,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":73.6,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.011797009823491633,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":30.9,"_gate_margins":0.009188002057085082,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":59.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02100451153077108,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.009225299576610668,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":38.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004885675200312683,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.0044400003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Axalta Coating Systems Ltd., through its subsidiaries, manufactures, markets, and distributes high-performance coatings systems in North America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia Pacific, and Latin America. The company operates through two segments, Performance Coatings and Mobility Coatings. It also offers water and solvent-borne products and systems to repair damaged vehicles for independent body shops, multi-shop operators, and original equipment manufacturers (OEM) dealership body shops. In addition, the company provides functional and decorative liquid, and powder coatings for building materials, cabinet, wood and luxury vinyl flooring, and furniture applications under the Imron Industrial, Tufcote Industrial, Corlar Industrial, Strenex Industrial, PercoTop, Voltatex, AquaEC, Durapon, Hydropon, UNRIVALED, Ceranamel, Alesta, Teodur, Nap-Gard, Abcite, and Plascoat brands. Further, it develops and supplies electrocoat, primer, the basecoat, and clearcoat products for OEMs of light and commercial vehicles; and coatings systems for various commercial applications, including HDT, MDT, bus, rail, motorcycles, marine and aviation, trailers, recreational vehicles, and personal sport vehicles under the Imron, Imron Elite, Centari, Rival, Corlar epoxy undercoats, and AquaEC brands. The company also offers products under the Audurra, Abcite, Alesta, AquaEC, Axalta Irus Mix, Axalta Irus Scan, Axalta NextJet, Axalta Nimbus, Centari, Ceranamel, Challenger, Chemophan, ColorNet, Cromax, Cromax Mosaic, Durapon 70, Duxone, Harmonized Coating Technologies, Hydropon, Imron ExcelPro, Imron Elite, Imron, Lutophen, Nap-Gard, Nason, Spies Hecker, Standox, Stollaquid, Syntopal, Syrox, Raptor, Rival, U-POL, and Vermeera brands. The company was formerly known as Axalta Coating Systems Bermuda Co., Ltd. and changed its name to Axalta Coating Systems Ltd. in August 2014. Axalta Coating Systems Ltd. was founded in 1866 and is headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chrishan Anthon Sebastian Villavarayan | CEO, President & Director | Age 55 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $423K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $37K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Axalta Coating Systems Ltd. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $7.9B market cap on $5.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $453M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.72\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.2\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 34% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.33794026597429694},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Basic Materials sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How (AXTA) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/38/How_AXTA_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_111926115801_1795150681.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795150681.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Paints and Coatings Market to Reach USD 293.54 Billion by 2035 as Waterborne and Powder Technologies, Asia Pacific Capacity and Industry Consolidation Reshape Competition","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/commodities/articles/paints-coatings-market-reach-usd-163400034.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795710840.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Axalta: 3 Key Takeaways for Long-Term Investors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/axalta-3-key-takeaways-long-015828834.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795658308.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"UK CMA Provisionally Approves Axalta and AkzoNobel Merger Remedy Package","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkine